Release Notes for Seq66 v. 0.99.27 2026-07-30 "Scratchpad Recording"

This version refactors the metronome code to support "scratchpad
recording", similar to background recording but with visual feedback.
Background recording when one wants to improvise.

Another "big" addition is a dialog for adding RPN/NRPN controls.

Also many fixes,
tweaks, and minor updates.

- Main window.
  Fixed disabling unavailable ports in the global buss dropdown.
- Pattern editor.
  - Fixed the left-align and right-align pattern-fix actions by
    bypassing initial meta events.
  - Added a dialog to provide a way to create an RPN and NRPN
    controller event in a pattern, or to add it as a MIDI
    macro.
- Event editor.
- Build system.
- Command-line.
- Miscellaneous.
  - Background recording. This feature has been fixed and upgraded to
    do "scratchpad recording". See the NEWS file and the user
    manual.
  - Port-mapping.
    - The Recreate button clears the port map and recreates it,
      including any devices plugged in while Seq66 runs.
- Documentation updated.

